      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high greatly increases the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common maximum dose.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg two or three times daily.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you intended. If 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that."
